<title>EGYPT: Egyptian firm buys 10,000 T yellow corn at $147.</title>
<headline>Egyptian firm buys 10,000 T yellow corn at $147.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian Starch and Glucose said on Sunday it bought 10,000 tonnes of yellow corn at 499.90 pounds ($147.25) a tonne for immediate delivery.</p>
<p>The seller was the local company Nefertiti and the corn was already in country, an ESGC official told Reuters.</p>
<p>($1 = 3.395 pounds)</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
